/* MJ-6 Unit II: ideal-gas and Carnot identities. */
kill(all)$
/* For one mole, Cp-Cv=R follows from H=U+RT. */
H : U(T)+R*T$
Cp : diff(H,T)$
Cv : diff(U(T),T)$
residual_Mayer : ratsimp(Cp-Cv-R);
/* Carnot cycle: Qh=R Th log(V2/V1), Qc=R Tc log(V3/V4) is the
   positive magnitude rejected to the cold reservoir,
   and the two adiabats give V3/V4=V2/V1. */
Qh : R*Th*log(r)$
Qc : R*Tc*log(r)$
eta : ratsimp((Qh-Qc)/Qh)$
residual_Carnot : ratsimp(eta-(1-Tc/Th));
/* Entropy mixing at equal T,P: sum n_i R ln(n/n_i). */
Smix : n1*R*log((n1+n2)/n1)+n2*R*log((n1+n2)/n2)$
residual_equal_amounts : ratsimp(subst(n2=n1,Smix)-2*n1*R*log(2));
